    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "types of effects are uncorrelated in the same individuals, $ \\sigma(\\mathrm{HS}) = \\sigma(z_{ijk}, z_{ij'k'}') = \\sigma^2(g_i) = \\sigma^2_{GCA} $. The SCA variance is equivalent to the covariance between full sibs minus twice $ \\sigma^2_{GCA} $, since $ \\sigma(\\mathrm{FS}) = \\sigma(z_{ijk}, z_{ijk'}') = 2\\sigma^2(g_i) + \\sigma^2(s_{ij}) = 2\\sigma^2_{GCA} + \\sigma^2_{SCA} $.",
