    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Diallel analysis is usually as concerned with the estimation of the $g_{i}$ and $s_{ij}$ values for the experimental lines as with the estimation of population components of variance. From Griffing (1956), the least-squares estimators of the effects and their standard errors are:",
